    "poster_id": 577459,
    "post_rendered": "In acute scalene triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"13\" >  the external angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\"  width=\"55\" height=\"13\" > meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"12\" > at point <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" >.</span>Lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd5977454df593c9bc9767f923da2ab880dd70f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/1/c516f91e65338e4dc2fc58c6303df7203c54e8ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" > which tangents of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > with respect to <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/5/5155aa866a797f98b826ed02392324eb8d7c0b5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ABC)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" >.</span>The line pass through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" > intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd5977454df593c9bc9767f923da2ab880dd70f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/1/c516f91e65338e4dc2fc58c6303df7203c54e8ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" > at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"12\" > respectively. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/0/7b0a6aebccd63e3eead091b60b01753d10705c57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(AYB)\\cap(AZC)=N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" > and <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/b/3eb71779ee44d276bb0b3730254a9df761c8278d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_b\\cap l_c=D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" >.</span> Show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/7/7778098e6f10ecdaf5eb74e56dcbfe099f22e785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ND$\"  width=\"31\" height=\"12\" > is angle bisector of <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/f/30f9a42fdbfc8f8a54efd518a9979cf7ec656170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle YNZ$\"  width=\"57\" height=\"12\" >.</span><br>\nProposed by <i>Alireza Haghi</i>",
    "post_canonical": "In acute scalene triangle $ABC$  the external angle bisector of $\\angle BAC$ meet $BC$ at point $X$.Lines $l_b$ and $l_c$ which tangents of $B$ and $C$ with respect to $(ABC)$.The line pass through $X$ intersects $l_b$ and $l_c$ at points $Y$ and $Z$ respectively. Suppose $(AYB)\\cap(AZC)=N$ and $l_b\\cap l_c=D$. Show that $ND$ is angle bisector of $\\angle YNZ$.\nProposed by [i]Alireza Haghi[/i]",
