    "topic_id": 2564031,
    "poster_id": 524450,
    "post_rendered": "Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" > is chosen on the Euler line of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"13\" > and it is inside of the triangle. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/0/250f765e0f0b3842f9d095dc0a3569905d344ce8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E,F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" > are were the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/2/6f2e1266e355231a44a30d03ef021f68d31446a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD,CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" > intersect with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/2/8327500afb9123f1b8bcfda5e3758342b848d8f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC,AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" > respectively. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" > is on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"13\" > such that <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/9/eb91db1725b76ea994c40eda87141d2244c24fba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EXF =180 - \\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"158\" height=\"13\" >,</span> also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/2385a638b5bcdefce880775acbb88396c59e61d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" > are on the same side of <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"12\" >.</span> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > is the second intersection of circumcircles of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddcabc9f05b9cca9f61fdb2145d38b2a52873a59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CXF,BXE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" > then prove the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/2/f4283acccd7ec13fb9e3a965f62da1edaf1be3d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XP,EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" > meet on the altitude of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"13\" ><br>\n<br>\nProposed by <i>Alireza Danaie</i>",
    "post_canonical": "Point $D$ is chosen on the Euler line of triangle $ABC$ and it is inside of the triangle. Points $E,F$ are were the line $BD,CD$ intersect with $AC,AB$ respectively. Point $X$ is on the line $AD$ such that $\\angle EXF =180 - \\angle A$, also $A,X$ are on the same side of $EF$. If $P$ is the second intersection of circumcircles of $CXF,BXE$ then prove the lines $XP,EF$ meet on the altitude of $A$ \n\nProposed by [i]Alireza Danaie[/i]",
