   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 22052575,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 2569765,
    "poster_id": 524450,
    "post_rendered": "Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" > is chosen inside the non trapezoid quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\"  width=\"57\" height=\"13\" > such that <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af2fa95083f9c4cca8c872a967fd98af1edd721e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AXD +\\angle BXC=180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"190\" height=\"14\" >.</span><br>\nSuppose the angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a462fa5c061d5837c8250bbc7380d7b02cb11738.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABX$\"  width=\"56\" height=\"13\" > meets the <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" >-</span>altitude of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/129af7ff8782b1a18bb903dcae920ddc278a2c46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADX$\"  width=\"44\" height=\"13\" > in <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\"  width=\"16\" height=\"12\" >,</span> and the angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/c/aac41999dec9f050e3cf0c475803a300fd130b92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DCX$\"  width=\"58\" height=\"12\" > meets the <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"13\" >-</span>altitude of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/129af7ff8782b1a18bb903dcae920ddc278a2c46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADX$\"  width=\"44\" height=\"13\" > in <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\"  width=\"12\" height=\"12\" >.</span>We know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/a/b1a250b1615ed6cd89dff8e2147dffd269cb3557.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BK \\perp CX$\"  width=\"85\" height=\"12\" > and <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/c/c1c1060c7aa4495bd052bcf264085bb2595c7022.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CL \\perp BX$\"  width=\"81\" height=\"12\" >.</span> If the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/129af7ff8782b1a18bb903dcae920ddc278a2c46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADX$\"  width=\"44\" height=\"13\" > is on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef091d889893c7c10e475a93e4ef626ff70aa5ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"12\" > prove that <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/a/bca70307969666e16938a8a8cd6a3cd04d553bcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL \\perp AD$\"  width=\"82\" height=\"13\" >.</span><br>\n<br>\nProposed by <i>Alireza Dadgarnia</i>",
    "post_canonical": "Point $X$ is chosen inside the non trapezoid quadrilateral $ABCD$ such that $\\angle AXD +\\angle BXC=180$. \nSuppose the angle bisector of $\\angle ABX$ meets the $D$-altitude of triangle $ADX$ in $K$, and the angle bisector of $\\angle DCX$ meets the $A$-altitude of triangle $ADX$ in $L$.We know $BK \\perp CX$ and $CL \\perp BX$. If the circumcenter of $ADX$ is on the line $KL$ prove that $KL \\perp AD$.\n\nProposed by [i]Alireza Dadgarnia[/i]",
    "username": "Mr.C",
    "post_number": 1,
    "post_format": "bbcode",
    "category_name": "High School Olympiads",
    "category_id": 6,
    "poster_avatar": "//avatar.artofproblemsolving.com/avatar_524450.jpeg?t=1599201444"
