    "topic_id": 2569761,
    "poster_id": 524450,
    "post_rendered": "Prove that we can color every subset with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" > element of a set with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a45e3d817886b4d9dbd6bb74ad23463ed139ed68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n$\"  width=\"19\" height=\"12\" > elements with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\"  width=\"8\" height=\"12\" > colors . In such a way that there are no  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\"  width=\"8\" height=\"12\" > subsets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a9874ea56cf8fec1bd246793224fbcfaad17ab3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" > with the same color where :<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e30c3802ee03d1b3929ab2253c83b9d46e7d7ed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"$$|A \\cap B| \\le 1,|A \\cap C| \\le 1,|B \\cap C| \\le 1$$\"  width=\"289\" height=\"18\" ><br>\nProposed by <i>Morteza Saghafian</i> and <i>Amir Jafari</i>",
    "post_canonical": "Prove that we can color every subset with $n$ element of a set with $3n$ elements with $8$ colors . In such a way that there are no  $3$ subsets $A,B,C$ with the same color where :\n$$|A \\cap B| \\le 1,|A \\cap C| \\le 1,|B \\cap C| \\le 1$$\n\nProposed by [i]Morteza Saghafian[/i] and [i]Amir Jafari[/i]",
